WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.161 --> 00:00:02.905
The seventh case is infinity to the power zero.

2
00:00:03.020 --> 00:00:04.975
Take x to the power one over x,

3
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:07.044
as x tends to positive infinity.

4
00:00:07.116 --> 00:00:09.803
The base grows while the exponent approaches zero.

5
00:00:09.954 --> 00:00:12.634
Again, call the expression y,

6
00:00:12.684 --> 00:00:15.756
and take its logarithm. ln y equals

7
00:00:15.756 --> 00:00:16.872
ln x divided by x.

8
00:00:17.122 --> 00:00:19.322
ln x divided by x tends to zero.

9
00:00:19.491 --> 00:00:23.408
Apply the exponential function to obtain the limit one.

10
00:00:23.544 --> 00:00:25.427
This result is specific to this example.

11
00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:27.090
You now have the seven cases.

12
00:00:27.239 --> 00:00:30.432
For quotients, try factorization or the dominant power.

13
00:00:30.568 --> 00:00:33.034
For differences of roots, the conjugate helps.

14
00:00:33.170 --> 00:00:35.564
For products, look for a suitable quotient.

15
00:00:35.712 --> 00:00:38.371
For powers with a positive base,

16
00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.400
use logarithms. Always identify the form,

17
00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:44.060
transform the expression, then calculate.
